From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:00:51 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro: give the UFS node a
 sleep pin state

The UFS host re-applies its pin state when it resumes with the link
down, so that the pads come back as the UFS function after a system
suspend (on the Pixel 9a they read as plain inputs on about one wake in
a hundred). pinctrl_select_state() does nothing for an unchanged state,
so the node needs a second state to switch away to: the "sleep" state
names the same pin groups as the default.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
index 4a1ea78aa..f6adcff16 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
@@ -1425,8 +1425,9 @@ ufs: ufs@13200000 {
 			phys = <&ufs_phy>;
 			phy-names = "ufs-phy";
 			samsung,sysreg = <&sysreg_ufs 0x710>;
-			pinctrl-names = "default";
+			pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&ufs_reset>, <&ufs_refclk>;
+			pinctrl-1 = <&ufs_reset>, <&ufs_refclk>;
 			lanes-per-direction = <2>;
 			dma-coherent;
 			status = "disabled";
